Title: "Disambiguates"
Id: "128951b9-c211-48a2-9a15-d54096d7ae2d"

Text: "`Disambiguates:` defines how an otherwise ambiguous operator or function-like
form should resolve globally.

```mlg-fragment
[FunctionOrOperatorForm]
Disambiguates:
(when: <ClauseUnion>+
 to: <Expression>)*
else?: <Expression>
Documented?: <DocumentedItemUnion>+
Justification?: <HaveGroup>+
Aliases?: <AliasItemUnion>+
Writing?: \"<WritingAlias>\"+
References?: <ResourceHeader>+
Metadata?: <MetadataItemUnion>+
Id?: <OpenText>
```

A `Disambiguates:` item must contain at least one `when:` / `to:` branch or an
`else:` section (or both). Each `when:` belongs to the `to:` that immediately
follows it; `else:` is the unconditional fallback.

```mlg-fragment
[x_ - y_]
Disambiguates:
else: x_ :-: y_
Documented:
. written: \"x_? - y_?\"
```

For a plain operator such as `x - y`, the checker first looks in local scope and
then in global definitions. If no definition is found and a matching
`Disambiguates:` entry exists, branches are tried in order. The first branch
whose `when:` requirements match supplies the `to:` expression. If no branch
matches, `else:` supplies the fallback expression.

The same rule applies to special operators, named infix operators, and
function-like notation. Each operator or function key may have at most one
`Disambiguates:` item."
Id: "3af69e35-73e0-4b8e-bedc-477b299d8cb8"
